  "source_text": "Title: Rotisserie-Style Chicken Gyros with Homemade Tzatziki\nServings: 4\n\nIngredients (component | amount unit | name | prep_style | pantry food_id):\n- Spiced Chicken | 500 g | chicken thigh |  | 000047\n- Spiced Chicken | 100 ml | Protein Yoghurt |  | 000641\n- Spiced Chicken | 30 g | lemon |  | 000130\n- Spiced Chicken | 20 ml | olive oil |  | 000378\n- Spiced Chicken | 1 tsp | Garlic Powder |  | 000643\n- Spiced Chicken | 1 tsp | Ground Onion |  | 000644\n- Spiced Chicken | 1 tsp | oregano |  | 000251\n- Spiced Chicken | 1 tsp | ground cumin |  | 000278\n- Spiced Chicken | 1 tsp | ground paprika |  | 000290\n- Spiced Chicken | 5 g | salted butter |  | 000211\n- Spiced Chicken | 2 g | ground black pepper |  | 000285\n- Homemade Tzatziki | 200 ml | Protein Yoghurt |  | 000641\n- Homemade Tzatziki | 1 pcs | Cucumber |  | 000642\n- Homemade Tzatziki | 10 g | garlic |  | 000112\n- Homemade Tzatziki | 5 g | dill |  | 000249\n- Homemade Tzatziki | 15 g | lemon |  | 000130\n- Pita and Assembly | 320 g | pita |  | 000340\n- Pita and Assembly | 100 g | lettuce |  | 000079\n- Pita and Assembly | 100 g | tomatoes |  | 000093\n- Pita and Assembly | 50 g | onion |  | 000111\n\nSteps in order (component | phase | minutes | text):\n1. Spiced Chicken | Prep |  | SAFETY: Wash hands before and after handling raw poultry. Slice chicken thighs into thin, 1cm strips.\n2. Homemade Tzatziki | Prep |  | Grate the cucumber using a box grater and place in a clean kitchen towel; squeeze forcefully to remove all liquid.\n3. Pita and Assembly | Prep |  | Thinly shred the lettuce and slice the tomatoes and onions into thin rounds or half-moons.\n4. Spiced Chicken | Prep |  | In a large mixing bowl, combine the yoghurt, lemon juice, olive oil, garlic powder, ground onion, oregano, cumin, and paprika.\n5. Homemade Tzatziki | Prep |  | Mince the fresh garlic and finely chop the dill leaves.\n6. Pita and Assembly | Cook |  | Heat a dry skillet over medium-high heat and warm each pita bread for about 45 seconds per side until soft and pliable.\n7. Spiced Chicken | Prep |  | Add the chicken to the marinade, ensure every piece is coated, and refrigerate for 30 minutes.\n8. Homemade Tzatziki | Prep |  | Whisk the yoghurt with the garlic, dill, and lemon juice until smooth.\n9. Pita and Assembly | Serve |  | Spread 2 tablespoons of tzatziki in the center of a warm pita.\n10. Spiced Chicken | Cook |  | Preheat your oven to 200°C and line a baking sheet with parchment paper.\n11. Homemade Tzatziki | Serve |  | Fold in the dry cucumber shreds and refrigerate until the chicken is ready.\n12. Pita and Assembly | Serve |  | Top with a handful of chicken, lettuce, tomatoes, and onions; roll tightly and serve immediately.\n13. Spiced Chicken | Cook |  | Spread the chicken in a tight single layer and roast for 20-25 minutes until deep brown and slightly charred at the edges.\n14. Spiced Chicken | Serve |  | Let the chicken rest for 5 minutes, then roughly chop it to create varying textures.",
